BERNOULLI AND EULER POLYNOMIALS, REIMANN ZETA FUNCTION (p.807)
23.2. Riemann Zeta Function and Other Sums of Reciprocal Powers
23.2.1 \ \gamma(s)=\sum_{k=1}^{\infty}k^{-s} \mathcal{R}s>1
23.2.2 =\Pi\ (1-p^{-s})^{-1} \mathcal{R}s>1
(product over all primes p).
23.2.3 =\frac{1}{s-1}+\frac{1}{2}+\sum_{k=1}^{\infty}\frac{B_{2k}}{2k}\left(\begin{pmatrix}s+2k-2\\ 2k-1\end{pmatrix}\right)^{\frac{1}{2}}\]
23.2.5 =\frac{1}{s-1}+\sum_{n=0}^{\infty}\frac{(-1)^{n}}{n!}\gamma_{n}(s-1)^{n} where
\gamma_{n}=\lim_{m\to n}\left\{\sum_{k=1}^{\infty}\frac{(\ln k)^{n}}{k}-\frac{(\ln m)^{n+1}}{n+1}\right\}\